{
 "summary": "Resolves Include-What-You-Use (IWYU) warnings across fuzz tests, fuzz utilities in `src/test/fuzz`, and several headers and modules in `src/`. Configures CI to treat IWYU warnings in these files as errors, and reformats the CI script's list of enforced files to one per line. It also maps standard C library cookie I/O functions in the IWYU mappings file.",
 "problem": "Fuzz targets and several core headers rely on transitive includes rather than directly declaring or including their dependencies. This prevents CI from enforcing IWYU rules on the fuzz test suite to prevent header hygiene regressions.",
 "evidence": [
  "Description notes this \"continues the ongoing effort to enforce IWYU warnings\" referencing the project's developer notes."
 ],
 "dependencies": {
  "depends_on": [
   "#36807",
   "#36844"
  ],
  "enables": []
 },
 "scope_notes": "Large mechanical change touching 189 files, consisting almost entirely of adding and removing `#include` statements and forward declarations.",
 "changed_since_previous": "Rebased on #36844, dropping the commit that consolidated duplicate `NodeId` declarations into `net_types.h`.",
 "card": "Fixes Include-What-You-Use (IWYU) warnings across fuzz tests in `src/test/fuzz` and select source headers, enabling strict CI error enforcement for them. It adjusts headers and forward declarations across nearly 190 files to eliminate reliance on transitive includes. This continues ongoing internal maintenance to automate include checking across the repository. The PR is a draft based on #36807 and #36844.",
